A||N||6||geezer||Optional wheel size for 88 GT||||1||
Z||000000||geezer||05-28-2000||11:18 AM||||Trying to figure out if it was possible to special order 14" wheels on '88 GT.  Want to run them as stock in autocross.  Anybody know if ordering them was possible?  Thanks for the help||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||05-28-2000||05:04 PM||||The offsets have been posted somewhere in another tire thread, but with specs in hand the correct wheels can be order from pretty much any wheel shop.<BR>On another note here is an unasked for consideration.<BR>Using 14" low profile tires to lower the vehicle will change the tire scrub.<BR>The ratio of suspension to tire edge changes the optimum offset.<BR>Since no money has been spent yet, advice from someone who has raced the same diameter tires could really improve handling for the same dollars.||||reg||12
Z||000002||sluppy123||05-28-2000||10:48 PM||||I think Geezer want's to know if Back in 88' you could special order a 88' fiero GT with 14" wheels from the factory.<P>I don't think it was possible because the wheels were part of the WS6 handling package standard of Gt's.<P>But what do I know, Just my .02-Brian<BR><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 05-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||05-28-2000||11:05 PM||||I have an order sheet from the dealer for 88 year model Fieros. The 14 in. wheels were not available on the GT because the diamond spoke 15's were standard equipment. Not to say that it could not have been done, but the order sheet doesnt show it as an option. The 15's were an option for Formulas, but so was the v6! Wouldnt you like to find that little old lady's low mileage Formula only to find that it was a 4cly with the 185/75 14's?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||05-29-2000||12:54 AM||||That's sort of right.....the Formula package was an option on the '88 coupe and it included the V-6, WS6 suspension, 120 MPH speedo & aux. gauge group & spoiler along with the 15" wheels.  You couldn't pick and choose what wheels to get with the Formula.....the 15's were standard on the Formula option group.  <P>Considering the Formula was only a $2000 option on the base coupe, it amazes me that more weren't built.  The base price of an '88 coupe was $8999 and the base Formula was $10,999.  Go figure?||||reg||6
Z||000005||Raydar||05-29-2000||11:06 PM||||Geezer, Do you think it might be legal to run 14's, since they were standard on the base coupe in 88? Or do the rules state specifically that they had to be available on the 88 GT? <BR>Many times, they will let you interchange parts that were available anywhere within the car line, from any year. <BR>Find out if you can use GT wheels from previous years. 85 GTs came *standard* with the same 14" wheel that you want to use.<BR>Rules can be interpreted in many ways. (nudge nudge. wink wink.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||05-29-2000||11:20 PM||||Raydar- you are probably right. I remember seeing later model z-28's with the old 82-84 style hoods. The 82 Z's had a fibreglass hood and folks would use them to save weight on their race cars. It looked strange to me seeing a 92 camaro with the 82 hood, but it was still legal.||||reg||1
